# Research

Handle $ARGUMENTS.

Resumable flow: `pick -> question -> registry -> queries -> leads -> read log -> score -> promote`. Never run benchmarks (`benchmark`), close issues row by row (`issue-harvester`, owner after `harvest --issues`), or patch code. `best-api` owns call shapes; Plan owns adoption. Discovery never auto-escalates into `audit`/`harvest`.

## Modes

| Arguments | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `<feature or question>` | Top open question -> discovery. |
| none | First unresearched scope (`node tooling/scripts/review-ledger.mjs due`). |
| `full <area>` | Ingest/compile every relevant corpus into `docs/research`. |
| `maintain <area>` | Repair lane (freshness, contradictions, backlinks, synthesis). |
| `audit [--target <surface\|full>] <repo>...` | Architecture comparison ([editor audit](./references/editor-audit.md); full/exhaustive/multi-repo uses Strict Source-to-Contract Matrix). |
| `audit sync [all\|<audit-id>\|<artifact-path>]...` | Refresh audits against newer commits ([editor audit](./references/editor-audit.md)). |
| `harvest <repo> [--since <commit>] [--issues ...] [--apply] [<filter>]` | Harvest portable behavior evidence ([test harvest](./references/test-harvest.md)). |
| `harvest plan <slate-v2\|plate> <report-or-repo-key>` or `harvest <report> --lane <lane>` | Lane adoption plan ([test harvest](./references/test-harvest.md)). |

Run `audit`/`harvest` only when requested after reading the linked reference in full. If the token after `audit`/`harvest` is not a repo, `owner/repo`, audit id, or report, treat `$ARGUMENTS` as a question.

## Pick what to research

1. Layer: `.agents/playbooks/references/architecture.md` (Pick the layer).
2. Known state: `node tooling/scripts/review-ledger.mjs lookup <scope-or-feature>` and `research <key-or-term>`; read `docs/plans/topics/<scope>.md`, `docs/research/sources/`, `docs/research/sources/editor-architecture/candidates.md`, `docs/research/sources/plate-notes/README.md`.
3. Priority: subject-file open question/`defer` limit > uncompared editor/lib > rejected lead with met reopen condition > changed source. State pick, layer, and why it beats runner-up.

Reuse matching reads/leads when question, revision, deps, and reopen condition match (inspect unknown provenance first); add support instead of duplicating. Lookups never advance Editor Audit cursors.

## Discovery run

Record question, scope, stop rule, artifact path, promotion owner, gap, exclusions first. Once per new task/verdict, run `pnpm kb discover <area>` (`docs/research/areas.tsv`, 10-min cap; lists repos missing from `docs/research/repos.tsv`; `--record` marks `skipped`).

Search web/GitHub (code, issues, PRs, benchmarks, browser fixtures, commits) across ProseMirror, Lexical, Tiptap, CodeMirror, Milkdown, Remirror, Monaco, Quill, ProseKit (extensions/adapters/autocomplete/UI), Meowdown (hybrid Markdown, hidden-syntax caret/selection, touch/IME/WebKit; desktop WebKit/touch emulation != iOS proof; separate ProseMirror code), virtualization/pagination libs, TS runtimes. Hits are leads only: inspect local source before claims, never copy code or patch from snippets/READMEs, translate into Plite/Plate model/change/selection/DOM/browser/proof terms.

### Artifacts, ledgers, and promotion

Store runs in main checkout's ignored `docs/plans/artifacts/<slug>/` (absolute path): `README.md`, `shards/NNN-<theme>.md`, `sources/`, and TSV ledgers:

- `repo-registry.tsv`: `repo_key, url, host, license, stars_or_signal, last_activity, topic_tags, local_path, status, score, notes`
- `query-ledger.tsv`: `query_key, surface, query, filters, result_count, sampled_count, new_repo_keys, new_lead_keys, next_query`
- `lead-ledger.tsv`: `lead_key, repo_key, source_ref, topic, claim, evidence_grade, novelty, applicability, proof_owner, next_action, status`
- `read-log.tsv`: `source_ref, repo_key, kind, path_or_url, lines_or_id, read_reason, takeaway, lead_key`
- `rejected-ledger.tsv`: `dedupe_key, repo_key, lead_key, reason, reopen_condition`
- `promoted-ledger.tsv`: `lead_key, packet_id, owner, test_or_benchmark, verification_command, decision`

New lead/read/promotion rows add `scope_id, review_id, source_revision, source_fingerprint, checked_at` (`unknown` if unavailable). Clone missing repos to `../<repo>` from main checkout (`../raw` = bulk corpora). `docs/research/raw`, `docs/research/probes`, `docs/plite/research` are frozen (`kb check` rejects additions). Keep dumps out of repo/chat; resume from `query-ledger.tsv` and `lead-ledger.tsv`.

Keys: `repo_key` = lowercase `host/owner/repo` (`repos.tsv`: `owner/name`), `query_key` = surface + query slug, `lead_key` = `<topic>:<normalized invariant>:<proof family>`, `dedupe_key` = normalized problem signature. Check `repos.tsv`, area pages, frozen runs, ledgers first. Shard 10-20 repos, 20-40 issues/PRs, or 1 theme; update ledgers per shard and stop early once a proof packet emerges.

- **Grades:** `A` (local source + runnable test/benchmark or exact behavior), `B` (detailed upstream issue/PR/discussion), `C` (docs/blog/example needing validation), `D` (search hit/README; next source only).
- **Score (`0-3`):** impact, novelty, applicability, proofability, risk; promote if `impact + novelty + applicability + proofability - risk >= 7` or active user bug. Prefer test/oracle/benchmark leads over runtime rewrites unless owner is proven.
- **Packets:** `test-packet` (unit/Playwright/Browser oracle + command), `benchmark-packet` (metric/runner repair + target + before/after command), `plan-packet` (`best-api` verdict + `.agents/playbooks/references/architecture.md` ledger row), `docs-packet` (`docs/research/sources/` citing `<owner>/<repo>@<commit>:<path>` or URL + date, or `docs/plans/topics/<scope>.md`), `no-code-decision` (rejected/quarantined on area page with reason, reopen condition, next angle).
- Update `docs/research/repos.tsv` (`saved`/`skipped` + `note`), write Stop/Pursue/Defer verdicts via `verdict` linked from subject file, and report counts (repos, issues/PRs, leads kept/merged/rejected, packets), top promoted leads (`lead_key`, grade, owner, proof command), key rejections, next shard or `none`.

## Compiled layer (`full` and `maintain`)

Read `docs/research/schema.md`, subject file, and `docs/research/sources/` first; drop to `..`, `../raw`, or external sources only to verify/resolve conflicts (primary outranks summaries). Acquire raw evidence: clones -> exports/caches -> captures (record URL/repo, raw path, date, revision); refresh only when active/drifted, appending `../raw/log.md` and updating compiled pages (never edit `../raw` while compiling).

Keep compiled pages derived (paraphrased synthesis, 1 concept/file, no silos like `editor-behavior/`/`plate-v2/`/`slate-v2/`), pointing claims outward. Route: findings -> `docs/research/sources/`, lessons -> `docs/research/sources/plate-notes/`, conclusions -> `docs/plans/topics/<scope>.md`, unresolved gaps -> open questions on blocked page, design questions -> `verdict` (`schema.md`), scratch -> `docs/analysis` or `docs/plans`.

- `full`: scope every corpus, check entrypoints, read strongest local raw hits before calling missing, explain skipped hits (grep = routing, never evidence; never spot-check one corpus as `full`), close each corpus with paths, read files, entrypoints, strongest evidence, next action, disposition (`evidenced`, `raw gap`, `compile gap`, `synthesis gap`, `freshness gap`, `evidence gap`, `contradiction gap`, `structure gap`).
- `maintain` (no area = repo-wide): fix stale claims, contradictions, orphan/duplicate/overgrown pages, dead terms, uncompiled raw evidence, implied decisions, answered questions; leave named open questions; report fixes/gaps/`full`/editor-behavior reconciliation needs; track setup workarounds; compile still-true lessons before retiring docs. Run before/after major research/migrations. Verify: `node tooling/scripts/review-ledger.mjs check` and `pnpm kb check`.

## Reading research ledgers

- Closing `docs/plite/research/**` leads: read `lead-ledger.tsv`, `promoted-ledger.tsv`, `read-log.tsv` first; use recorded refs/owners before repo-wide `rg`.
- Prefer literal `status` over `decision`/`action`/regex; never infer backlog from `decision` when `status` exists.
- Parse work ledgers only (`lead-ledger.tsv`, `promoted-ledger.tsv`, issue closure ledgers, action matrices), never metadata (`repo-registry.tsv`, `read-log.tsv`).
- Buckets: actionable (`promote-*`, `promoted-pending`, `queued-*`, `open`, `todo`, `candidate`, `needs-*`, untriaged), closed (`promoted-kept`, `promoted-existing`, `kept-*`, `covered`, `covered-existing`, `supporting`, `supporting-only`, `invalid-skip`, `rejected`, `closed`), deferrals (`deferred-*`, legacy `defer`).
- Print TSV headers or JSON keys before writing a reducer (`check`, not `checked`).
